    "status": "present",
    "value": "Count distinct permutations in which every adjacent sum is a perfect square; duplicate input values must not duplicate counts. The approach is: sorted-index bitmask DP on square-sum adjacency; canonical duplicate consumption avoids overcount. Its target cost is O(n^2*2^n) time/O(n*2^n) space. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
